From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:02:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 85/94] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm630: Add the CPU BWMON

Since the interconnect providers sync their state, the BIMC runs at
what its consumers vote, down to the 19.2 MHz keep_alive floor. The
CPUs vote nothing, so CPU-bound work gets whatever DDR rate the GPU,
display and DMA masters happen to ask for. Downstream scales DDR for
the CPU with the bandwidth monitor at the start of the BIMC block
(qcom,bimc-bwmon4, port 0, SPI 183) driving the cpubw devfreq device,
whose vote is active-only.

Describe the same monitor for the mainline icc-bwmon driver. It votes
on the APSS -> EBI path with RPM_ACTIVE_TAG, so the vote only lands in
the RPM active set and drops out when the APSS power-collapses; it
must not hold DDR in the sleep set.

The OPP table is the downstream cpubw qcom,bw-tbl (MiB/s, SDM660),
starting at the 762 MiB/s (200 MHz) min_freq the downstream init
script (init.qcom.post_boot.sh, sdm660 branch) sets for cpubw;
381 and 572 MiB/s are never voted there. Downstream devbw votes
ib = MiB/s * 2^20 B/s, and both msm_bus and icc-rpm divide the peak
by the 4-byte EBI width to get the BIMC rate, so each OPP is written
as MiB/s * 1048576 / 1000 kB/s: the same RPM request downstream sends
(762 -> ~200 MHz ... 6881 -> ~1804 MHz). The GPU OPPs in this file
already vote 768/1017/1296/1353 MHz the same way (MHz * 4000 kB/s).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi | 66 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 66 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
index 29913c23b..d4e9813cd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm630.dtsi
@@ -627,6 +627,72 @@ rng: rng@793000 {
 			clock-names = "core";
 		};
 
+		pmu@1008000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,sdm660-cpu-bwmon", "qcom,msm8998-bwmon";
+			reg = <0x01008000 0x300>, <0x01001000 0x200>;
+			reg-names = "monitor", "global";
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 183 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+
+			operating-points-v2 = <&cpu_bwmon_opp_table>;
+			interconnects = <&gnoc MASTER_APSS_PROC RPM_ACTIVE_TAG
+					 &bimc SLAVE_EBI RPM_ACTIVE_TAG>;
+
+			/*
+			 * Downstream cpubw bw-tbl in MiB/s, from the 762 MiB/s
+			 * (200 MHz) min_freq its init script sets for SDM660.
+			 * Downstream votes MiB/s * 2^20 B/s over the 4-byte EBI,
+			 * so the same peak in kB/s asks the RPM for the same
+			 * BIMC rate.
+			 */
+			cpu_bwmon_opp_table: opp-table {
+				compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+				opp-0 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(762 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-1 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(1144 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-2 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(1571 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-3 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(2086 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-4 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(2597 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-5 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(2929 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-6 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(3879 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-7 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(4943 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-8 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(5163 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-9 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(5931 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+
+				opp-10 {
+					opp-peak-kBps = <(6881 * 1048576 / 1000)>;
+				};
+			};
+		};
+
 		bimc: interconnect@1008300 {
 			compatible = "qcom,sdm660-bimc";
 			reg = <0x01008300 0x77d00>;
